    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="0610" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg530"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Raikes to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-24"><hi rendition="#italic">May 24,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hay</hi>: I have informed Lord Lansdowne by
                    telegraph of the offer which the President has made to send home the remains of
                    Lord Pauncefote in a vessel of the American Navy as a testimony of respect, and
                    I have asked him whether I may accept his offer on benalf of Lady
                    Pauncefote.</p>
                <p>Yours, very sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur S. Raikes.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
